{"content_hash": "3f3927cfd9c89b42", "version_id": 653, "article_id": 66, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Apple launches HomeView, a smart home hub with new Siri AI", "title_zh": "苹果发布HomeView智能家居中控，搭载全新Siri AI", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/13/apple-new-smart-home-device-ai", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585184394271-4c0a47dc59c9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8YXBwbGUlMjB1bnZlaWxzJTIwc21hcnR8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MTkzNzgwMHww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Laurenz Heymann on Unsplash", "author": "Laurenz Heymann", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@lagommedia?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/apple-logo-on-glass-window-wAygsCk20h8?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(188, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(226, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "a8145be00b2e"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-14", "word_count": 140, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "Apple has introduced a new smart home device called HomeView, which works as a hub for other gadgets. It also updated Siri with AI to make it more useful.", "lead_zh": "苹果推出了一款名为HomeView的新智能家居设备，可以作为其他智能设备的控制中心。苹果还用AI升级了Siri，让它更好用。", "preview": "On Tuesday, Apple showed off new smart home products, including the HomeView, an iPad-like device that can hang on walls or sit on tables. I", "preview_zh": "周二，苹果展示了新的智能家居产品，包括HomeView。这款类似iPad的设备可以挂在墙上或放在桌上。起售价299美元，下个月开始发货。今天开始预售，11月13日正式上市。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 636, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/66/en_b1.wav", "duration": 53.4, "size_bytes": 2568044, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 163, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@f606c78/content/data/versions/653.json", "paragraphs": ["On Tuesday, Apple showed off new smart home products, including the HomeView, an iPad-like device that can hang on walls or sit on tables. It starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. Preorders start today, and the device will be available from 13 November.", "The HomeView has a 7-inch screen and face recognition. It helps users control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks. Apple also updated its HomePod speaker and Apple TV, and introduced accessories from LG and Schneider Electric, such as cameras, a thermostat and a smart lock.", "However, the HomeView will not be sold in the European Union because Siri AI is not available there due to EU rules. Apple first released its Home app in 2016, but it has struggled to compete with Amazon and Google. Now, new AI companies like OpenAI are also making hardware."], "paragraphs_zh": ["周二，苹果展示了新的智能家居产品，包括HomeView。这款类似iPad的设备可以挂在墙上或放在桌上。起售价299美元，下个月开始发货。今天开始预售，11月13日正式上市。", "HomeView配有7英寸屏幕和面部识别功能，能帮助用户控制门铃、恒温器和智能锁。苹果还更新了HomePod音箱和Apple TV，并推出了LG和施耐德电气的配件，比如摄像头、恒温器和智能锁。", "不过，由于欧盟规定，Siri AI在欧洲不可用，所以HomeView不会在欧盟销售。苹果早在2016年就推出了家庭App，但在与亚马逊和谷歌的竞争中一直不太成功。现在，像OpenAI这样的新AI公司也在做硬件。"], "body": "On Tuesday, Apple showed off new smart home products, including the HomeView, an iPad-like device that can hang on walls or sit on tables. It starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. Preorders start today, and the device will be available from 13 November.\n\nThe HomeView has a 7-inch screen and face recognition. It helps users control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks. Apple also updated its HomePod speaker and Apple TV, and introduced accessories from LG and Schneider Electric, such as cameras, a thermostat and a smart lock.\n\nHowever, the HomeView will not be sold in the European Union because Siri AI is not available there due to EU rules. Apple first released its Home app in 2016, but it has struggled to compete with Amazon and Google. Now, new AI companies like OpenAI are also making hardware.", "body_zh": "周二，苹果展示了新的智能家居产品，包括HomeView。这款类似iPad的设备可以挂在墙上或放在桌上。起售价299美元，下个月开始发货。今天开始预售，11月13日正式上市。\n\nHomeView配有7英寸屏幕和面部识别功能，能帮助用户控制门铃、恒温器和智能锁。苹果还更新了HomePod音箱和Apple TV，并推出了LG和施耐德电气的配件，比如摄像头、恒温器和智能锁。\n\n不过，由于欧盟规定，Siri AI在欧洲不可用，所以HomeView不会在欧盟销售。苹果早在2016年就推出了家庭App，但在与亚马逊和谷歌的竞争中一直不太成功。现在，像OpenAI这样的新AI公司也在做硬件。", "text": "On Tuesday, Apple showed off new smart home products, including the HomeView, an iPad-like device that can hang on walls or sit on tables. It starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. Preorders start today, and the device will be available from 13 November. The HomeView has a 7-inch screen and face recognition. It helps users control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks. Apple also updated its HomePod speaker and Apple TV, and introduced accessories from LG and Schneider Electric, such as cameras, a thermostat and a smart lock. However, the HomeView will not be sold in the European Union because Siri AI is not available there due to EU rules. Apple first released its Home app in 2016, but it has struggled to compete with Amazon and Google. Now, new AI companies like OpenAI are also making hardware.", "vocab": [{"word": "unveil", "pos": "verb", "zh": "发布，推出", "note": "常用于新产品或计划的首次公开", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "smart home", "pos": "noun", "zh": "智能家居", "note": "指能联网控制的家庭设备", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "hub", "pos": "noun", "zh": "中心，枢纽", "note": "这里指控制其他设备的中心设备", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "preorder", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "预售，预订", "note": "在产品正式发售前下单购买", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "face recognition", "pos": "noun", "zh": "面部识别", "note": "通过人脸识别身份的技术", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "thermostat", "pos": "noun", "zh": "恒温器", "note": "控制室内温度的装置", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "accessory", "pos": "noun", "zh": "配件，附件", "note": "常指附加的设备或物品", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fend off", "pos": "phrasal verb", "zh": "抵挡，抵御", "note": "常与竞争、攻击等搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "regulation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "法规，规定", "note": "政府或机构制定的规则", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "conversational", "pos": "adj", "zh": "对话式的，口语化的", "note": "形容AI能像人一样对话", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Apple unveils new smart home devices that showcase upgraded Siri AI", "summary_original": "New products from Apple include the HomeView, an iPad-like device that acts as a hub for other smart home gadgets\nApple on Tuesday began showing off a ⁠new round of smart home products, including an iPad-like device dubbed the HomeView, meant to hang on walls or perch on tabletops ⁠and act as a hub for other smart home devices.\nThe HomeView device starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. It will feature a 7in screen and face recognition, will help users ⁠control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks in a market where Apple has tinkered for a decade without major success. The device will also showcase Apple’s AI-upgraded Siri virtual ​assistant.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Apple unveils new smart home devices that showcase upgraded Siri AI\nNew products from Apple include the HomeView, an iPad-like device that acts as a hub for other smart home gadgets\nApple on Tuesday began showing off a ⁠new round of smart home products, including an iPad-like device dubbed the HomeView, meant to hang on walls or perch on tabletops ⁠and act as a hub for other smart home devices.\nThe HomeView device starts at $299 and will begin shipping next month. It will feature a 7in screen and face recognition, will help users ⁠control doorbells, thermostats and smart locks in a market where Apple has tinkered for a decade without major success. The device will also showcase Apple’s AI-upgraded Siri virtual ​assistant.\nPreorders begin today and the devices are expected to be available starting 13 November.\nApple is launching these products as it ⁠tries to fend off competition from rivals, including traditional competitors like Amazon – which has invested heavily in ​its Echo speakers and Ring doorbells and ‌last week launched premium tablets – as well as newer AI upstarts like OpenAI that have hardware ambitions of their own.\nApple’s HomeView launch was accompanied by updates to its HomePod smart speaker and Apple TV devices. It also introduced a range of ‌accessories, including doorbells, cameras and thermostats, made by LG and Schneider Electric and designed with help from Apple.\nThe new line of devices are accessible and managed in the Apple home app. The accessories include a Schneider smart thermostat and LG home security devices including indoor and various outdoor cameras including a doorbell camera and floodlight camera as well as a smart lock. The lock can be unlocked using the Apple home app.\nThe HomeView device will not be sold in the European Union, because Siri AI remains unavailable there due to EU regulations, Apple said.\nApple first released its Home app to control smart gadgets in 2016, ⁠with HomePod smart speakers following in 2018, but those offerings are competing with ​Alphabet’s Google Home speakers and ​Amazon’s Echo line. Analysts said ​two major hurdles for Apple were making its devices work with a ​variety of third-party gadgets and ‌the limited ability ​of Siri to ​give useful answers.\nThe HomeView device includes a revamped version of Siri AI, the company announced. An Apple press release described the new version of Siri as more capable and conversational, using information from personal apps like Messages and Calendar to provide more relevant answers.\n“It’s powered by Apple Intelligence with Siri AI at its core, drawing on personal context from your iPhone to help you find what you need and get more done, all while keeping everyone’s information private and secure,” the release said.\nExplore more on these topics\nApple\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "202